      "description": "Watch CSKA 1948 vs Panathinaikos highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 11, 2026. On August 11, 2026 , the UEFA Conference League witnessed a tactical chess match between CSKA 1948 and Panathinaikos , where endurance and strategic depth were put to the ultimate test. The contest evolved into a grueling battle that kept spectators guessing until the very last whistle. Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Half The first half was characterized by physical play and defensive discipline, as both sides struggled to find a clinical edge in the final third. Panathinaikos attempted to control the tempo through midfield possession, but they were often met by a resilient CSKA 1948 backline. The intensity of the match was highlighted in the 41st minute when Georgios Katris received a yellow card for a robust challenge. Both teams headed into the locker rooms at halftime with the scoreline deadlocked, reflecting the high stakes of the competition. Goals and Late Drama The match burst into life in the second half. In the 60th minute, Levi Garcia broke the deadlock for Panathinaikos with a clinical strike, sparking a series of tactical adjustments from both benches. As the pressure mounted, the referee was kept busy, issuing yellow cards to Elmin Rastoder and Moataz Zemzemi . Just as it appeared the visitors would escape with a narrow victory, CSKA 1948 found a lifeline in the 87th minute. Lasha Dvali powered home a late equalizer, sending the home crowd into raptures and forcing the match into extra time. Extra-Time Decider With legs tiring, the first half of extra time proved decisive. In the 95th minute, Giorgos Kyriakopoulos provided a pinpoint assist for Cyriel Dessers , who finished calmly to restore the lead for Panathinaikos . Despite a flurry of late substitutions, including the introduction of Dragan Grivic and Florian Krebs , CSKA 1948 could not find a second equalizer. A late booking for Frederic Maciel in the 112th minute underscored the frantic closing stages, but Panathinaikos held their nerve to secure a hard-fought victory."
